WEBVTT

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.350
Why do I have to guard some little girl?!

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:13.180
She's not just some girl.
She's Mario Bossi's daughter.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.620
Eh?

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.460
We can't afford to have her
get kidnapped during the trial.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.830
But you don't need a cyborg like me for that.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.960
She's a regular girl just about your age.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.830
Spending time with her
will be a good experience.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.830
I'm not a regular girl!

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.010
That didn't go well.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.180
All she does is say, "Let me train more!"

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.910
Because of the Pinocchio incident?

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.320
Yeah. Her defeat's been pretty hard on her.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.320
She is a very proud girl...

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.920
Who is this daughter of Mario Bossi?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.320
She's his common-law daughter.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.860
She lives alone in Naples.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.850
The public doesn't know about her,
but we're not taking chances...

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:07.200
Giuse-san. I want to show her
more of the world, not just fighting.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.010
I'm home, Augustus.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.120
It looks like I have to meet
Mario's daughter tomorrow.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:26.420
Hirscher and I had another argument.
Even though I don't want to.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:37.640
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:51.110
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:01:52.680 --> 00:02:00.160
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:07.430
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:17.840
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:25.250
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:32.860
I want to protect the only one for me

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:40.660
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:48.040
Amid the eternal love I feel simply by living,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:56.880
I want to fulfill my promise

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:04.890
"The Hague, Netherlands"

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.490
"Europol Headquarters"

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.060
"Europol Headquarters"
You want field work?

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.390
You want field work?

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.560
Sorry, Hartmann.
There is other work for you to do.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.400
Do you mean traveling to Paris,
Rome, Lisbon, and everywhere else

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.440
to visit with police officials?

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.770
That's right.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.840
The Europol is like the European FBI,

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.950
but is hated by police
organizations everywhere.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.580
Establishing friendly relationships
with them is a very important job.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.750
But, sir!

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:39.250
1.5 million girls are illegally
bought and sold worldwide every year!

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.070
Please let me join the task force!

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:49.790
"Flowers of Good Will"

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.170
Hartmann. About our
conversation the other day...

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.340
I appreciate your passion,
but I just can't give you field work.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.580
Why not?!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.780
It's at the request of the
German police who sent you here.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.050
What the hell does that matter?!

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.620
Refine your diplomatic
skills and your connections.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.290
Do that, and you'll make it big
in life, both here and back home.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.990
You can realize your ideals after that.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.090
Here.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.610
What's this?

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.080
The scene of a child abuse incident.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.810
Watch it and think things over.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.920
Know what a snuff movie is?

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.390
It's a video of a murder,
meant for entertainment.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.620
Huh?

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:51.900
People take kids they abduct or
buy and film them being killed.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.730
You can't be serious...

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.900
Some are fakes, many are shams.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:04.440
But, just as you say,
human trafficking goes on every year,

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:09.610
and many go missing or
are found as cut-up corpses.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:13.520
A small percentage of cases are deemed as real.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.260
This is reality.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.930
Our world is filled with evil.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:31.540
Until you can accept that fact,
I can't send you on field investigations.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:38.070
You're blessed.
You grew up believing that people are good.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:56.050
"Naples, Campania"

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:02.470
Hi! I'm Maria Machiavelli!

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.970
Victor Hirscher. This is Triela.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.070
Ciao!

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.010
Nice to meet you...

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.710
We'll be your security until
your father's done testifying.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.350
Uhh...

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.520
What about when I want
to hit the town and stuff?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.920
For your security,
it's best if you refrain from going outside.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.750
Eh?!

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.200
I'm going to the Naples D.A.
I leave you in charge here.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.670
In charge? When are you coming back?

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:38.200
The beginning of next week.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:43.330
Don't worry. Olga's team
will be staying here, too.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.710
Say!

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.710
Yes?

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.240
I hear you're a professional killer?

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.290
Yes.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.290
Show me something!

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.090
Okay...

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:13.900
Awesome!

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.440
Say, Triela.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:18.710
Yes?

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:20.540
What's your hobby?

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.210
Hobby?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.920
Mine's soccer. I even play it myself.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.590
You don't have one? Do you collect anything?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.790
Oh!

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.320
Uhh... teddy bears...

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.100
Tadah!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:47.000
Daddy gives me one every once in a while!

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:52.940
Pepino, Gaetano, Jacinto, Zoff, Bobo.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:08:00.180
And this is Alex. I got him
last Christmas. He's a forward!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:04.690
I have the same one!
Mario gave me one last Christmas, too!

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.950
Oh? What's yours named?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.730
Augustus.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.260
That's a strong-sounding name!
What position does he play?

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.600
Eh?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:24.480
I heard from Hirscher that you
saved my daddy this past Christmas.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.810
Yeah.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.450
Say, Maria-san. Do you...

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.650
Call me Mimi.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.720
Do you love your father, Mimi?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.490
Mario said he hasn't seen
his daughter in a long time...

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.820
You don't hold a grudge against him?

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:47.420
He's my daddy! Of course I love him!

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.360
That's a relief.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:55.040
I finally feel like I was useful for once.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.770
I've been depressed lately
because I messed up at work...

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.010
It sounds like you really have it rough.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:07.550
What about you, Mimi?
Isn't it hard living all by yourself?

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:12.180
Not at all! Every day is
a blast for me! I'm very happy!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:25.600
Checking over and over
won't change it, Pauline.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.570
She died of asphyxiation from strangulation.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:31.440
Her killer was a large man.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.070
Yes.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:46.020
I'm sorry, Rachelle. Agent Alain
kept pestering us to check again.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:50.390
Is he suggesting it's the M.E.S'
fault the investigation's at a standstill?

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.600
Don't be like that!
He's trying his hardest, too!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.270
Why don't you meet him?
He'd be a good catch!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.700
No, I'm fine.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.570
You need to care more
about meeting people!

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:05.470
You won't have a chance
when you're middle-aged!

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:11.050
Meeting? You might be right...

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.560
Victor Hartmann?

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.500
Oh, aren't you with the Paris police?

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.230
I'm Rachelle Belleut.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.100
We're on the same floor,
but this is the first time we've spoken.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.590
Do you need something from me?

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.910
I was hoping we could talk...

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:41.430
Do you have plans this weekend?

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:52.660
My job is to determine the
cause of the children's deaths.

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:57.460
This one died of blood loss,
this one was asphyxiated...

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.430
But the investigations
never make any progress.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:03.670
Even when there's
information about human trafficking,

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:08.010
the Europol has almost no
authority in whatever place it's happening.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:11.070
Oh, I'm sorry!
I'm the only one who's been talking...

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:13.940
No, that's okay.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:20.350
I'm not a very considerate woman.
I hardly ever dine with men...

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:24.390
I even had to borrow these clothes
and this perfume from a coworker.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.190
It's been a long time for me, too.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:31.650
I only get to dine during business
meetings while I'm traveling around.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.840
The chief got on my case the other day.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.510
Said I knew too little about the real world.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:47.470
It's true. I underestimated how
bad the child abuse situation is!

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:53.780
I had no idea that people
were so driven by evil.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:58.160
I couldn't believe it, either!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:04.830
Until I joined the Europol,
I had never seen such horrifying corpses!

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:10.460
And the way I grow
accustomed to them terrifies me...

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.210
Tell me, Hartmann-san.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.140
What will you do when you
learn about the real world?

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:21.280
Lose all hope and return to Germany?

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:27.620
No. I plan to bargain with the
chief so I can do actual field work.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.790
I want to believe that the
world hasn't been forsaken!

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:34.190
I have to help the children!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:40.060
Umm, I heard this
from an Italian investigator...

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:42.970
The Naples mafia has recently started

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:46.640
a human trafficking business in Amsterdam.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.270
We can't investigate officially...

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:53.770
...but we could both go there, if you'd like.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:08.190
Oh? Chianti Classico
Riserva, Machiavelli, huh?

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:13.100
Daddy gave me a case of it just
because it matches my last name.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.730
Niccolo Machiavelli's
descendants made this wine, you know.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.640
Really?

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.510
Who's he again?

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:22.740
Triela.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.780
A medieval philosopher.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.010
He said, "One must be
a fox to recognize traps,

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:29.450
and a lion to frighten wolves."

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.950
Precisely. Very impressive, Triela.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:36.150
No, it was nothing...

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.130
Checkmate.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:55.900
You're so good at games, Triela.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.840
Want to play table soccer again?

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:04.650
No, thanks. I haven't stood a
chance for three days straight now.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:10.150
Hey, let's play real soccer outside!
I think I could beat you in that!

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:13.260
You can't. The trial is still going on.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:19.300
Eh?! I wanna see my sweetheart! Please!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:21.260
You text-message him all the time as it is.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:26.200
I wanna see him! I wanna see
him and hug him and kiss him!

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.780
C'mon... Can't you
persuade Hirscher for me?

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.010
N-No.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.740
Cheapskate.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:40.850
Say, Triela...

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:41.950
Yeah?

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:45.580
You love Hirscher, don't you?

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.020
What makes you say that?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.660
It's obvious enough.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.700
Say, have you confessed your love?

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:58.300
Of course not. Because not
even I know if I love him or not...

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:02.870
Besides, in either case, we
couldn't have a relationship like that.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:07.040
What's so wrong with teacher
and student, superior and subordinate?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:10.180
Just look into his eyes and say, "Tiamo!"

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.650
And then everything'll be A-OK!

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:15.950
Yeah. You might be right.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:24.360
Triela seems like an ordinary
girl when she's with Mimi like that.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.060
She really does.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.700
What I've learned from
living with her for several days

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:36.470
is that cyborgs really are
different from regular girls after all.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:43.950
I know marksmanship,
martial arts, lock-picking...

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:48.250
I don't know anything about
the latest music or television shows.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:52.650
Which means what I'm supposed to do is...

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:56.350
"Naples District Attorney's Office"

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:01.430
I appreciate everything you've
done for my daughter, Hirscher.

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:02.370
It's no problem.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.100
But I'm glad to hear the
trial should end without incident.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:09.540
I just hope this makes at least
some amends for my past sins...

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.280
So, what do you plan to do next, Mario?

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.110
Escape overseas, like always.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.610
I figure Mimi will want to stay in Naples,

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.620
so I won't be able to
see her again for a while.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:20.620
I see.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:23.620
Give Triela-jouchan my regards...

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:29.680
No, never mind. I am a pretty
bad guy in her eyes, after all.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:35.190
"Amsterdam, Netherlands"

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:41.200
Do you think that Naples mobster
named Mario was telling the truth?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:45.810
He did seem opposed to the
group's human trafficking from the start.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:50.210
He regretted being an
accomplice to this business.

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:54.650
And snuff movies are made inside there?

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.960
Rachelle. You should stay here...

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:02.660
No, I'm coming.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:06.490
I don't want to see
children's corpses anymore.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:22.580
So this is how painful bullet wounds are...

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:26.680
Hold on, Rachelle!
Let's get outside and call the police!

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:32.520
We still haven't... found the
children... We have to help them...

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:38.220
There's a light!

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.830
Wait here, Rachelle!

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:51.680
Know what a snuff movie is?

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:55.910
It's a video of a murder,
meant for entertainment.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:18:01.550
People take kids they abduct or
buy and film them being killed.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:29.480
This is reality. Our world is filled with evil.

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:31.880
Rachelle!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.220
Keep watch in the hallway, Hartmann...

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.450
Rachelle!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:41.880
She's still alive. I have to save her...

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.560
Hartmann...

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:49.530
I didn't want to believe it either...

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:54.440
I had no idea the real
world was this revolting...

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:59.010
We've let countless children die in the past...

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:03.580
But... if I can at least save this girl...

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:08.220
...I think I'll be able to believe
the world hasn't been forsaken,

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:11.350
just as you said...

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.490
Right, Victor?!

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:18.830
What?!

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:22.230
Our world hasn't been forsaken!

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:25.930
It's just as you said!

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.710
No, it hasn't been!

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:35.080
Because there are wonderful
doctors like you in the world, Rachelle!

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:49.730
Rachelle!

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:53.790
Rachelle! Rachelle! Rachelle!

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:14.950
What do you call that?!

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:17.020
You're a disgrace to our special forces unit!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.790
Put your equipment on and go
run 10 kilometers! On the double!

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.320
Yes, sir!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.160
- Triela.
- Yes?

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.760
My men are pathetic.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:28.430
You must be disappointed
he didn't put up a fight.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:31.490
No, not at all...

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.710
Listen, men!

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:43.710
This is what happens

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:46.580
when even the toughest
soldier is caught off guard!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.220
Never lower your guard,
regardless of the enemy's form!

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:53.460
I take it that until now,
you've always relied on your body's abilities

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.860
to overwhelm your opponents.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:59.990
That's why you lost to this Pinocchio fellow.

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:13.140
Was that what you wanted?
Isn't she an important subordinate?

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:17.510
Yes. I called you here to make her feel pain.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:21.480
She can't train with agency
members because of her conditioning,

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.050
plus we don't have any experts like you.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:27.490
It'll be good training for my men, too.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:31.090
Terrorists aren't always
adults these days, after all.

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:33.900
Don't worry. In two weeks

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:38.100
I'll have changed that bunny
rabbit into an unstoppable force.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:41.660
Yes. I appreciate it.

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:55.850
- Have you put her under?
- Yes.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:01.420
Then we'll begin her routine leg replacement.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.730
This new leg has better
performance than the previous one.

00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:05.800
Is that so?

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:08.570
Development has gone much more smoothly

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:12.160
ever since we were
allowed to use Claes for tests.

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:22.410
Donato-san!

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:23.480
What is it?

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:26.880
This cyborg... is crying!

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:30.290
- Wipe them away.
- Sir?

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:36.280
Wipe her tears. They shed
them while they sleep.

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:48.810
Awake?

00:22:48.810 --> 00:22:51.470
We've finished your routine maintenance.

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:54.570
You can leave if you can walk.

00:22:58.150 --> 00:23:01.550
What's wrong? Did you have a bad dream?

00:23:04.390 --> 00:23:07.260
I don't really remember...

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:10.860
But it was a kind dream...

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:15.520
In it, I met my mother...

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:23.110
She was wearing glasses,
and had a nice-smelling perfume on...

00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:29.010
And then she gently embraced me...

00:23:45.660 --> 00:24:00.740
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:10.090
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:18.260
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:26.240
though they can't be put into words

00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:34.340
I'll summon all my strength

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:46.880
to know what it means to live

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:06.020
"Budding Feelings"
